---
import Chart from "./Chart.astro";
---

<section class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="hero-title pixel-heading">ASCIICHARTS</h1>
    <p class="hero-tagline pixel-heading" style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--fg);">
      How to build charts out of text characters — right
    </p>
    <p class="hero-pitch">
      For the places images can't go: PR descriptions, incident channels, CI logs, commit messages,
      terminals — and the replies of AI agents. <strong>The principles</strong> say how to get every
      cell right; <strong>a skill</strong> teaches agents to draw by them; <strong>two reference
      implementations</strong>, Go and Python, render them byte for byte.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn btn-primary pixel-corners" href="#principles">
        THE PRINCIPLES ▸
      </a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary pixel-corners" href="#ways-in">
        GET STARTED
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-chart">
      <Chart id="hero" kind="hbar · grouped" />
      <p class="hero-chart-caption">
        Real <code>render_chart()</code> output, frame and title included — flip{" "}
        <strong>MONO / COLOR</strong> or <strong>BLACK / WHITE</strong> right on the chart.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
